# When they say all

- Treat "all", "all roles", "everything", "full review", and "etc" as every applicable role plus each language already in the project.
- Read one role or language `SKILL.md` at a time. Those files are not already in context.
- Skip a role that has nothing to inspect. Do not invent a stack.
- Propose durable findings as rules under `.cursor/rules/` in the project being reviewed.
- Ask whether to add a new rule, modify an existing one, or skip. Write a file only after they choose.

```text
BAD:  Write the rule files before asking.
GOOD: List add and modify proposals, then write only the ones the user accepts.
```
